IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-interpretation`
IMPORT `g6-art18-governor-duties`
IMPORT `g6-art20-court-orders`

-- g6-art19-reportable-matters.l4 (imports g6-art20-court-orders for the record `Disqualification order`, which Article 20(3) creates and Article 19(1)(b) reads): Article 19 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Reportable matters and acting as a governor.
-- The survey proposed one module for Articles 19 and 20 (`g6-art19-20-fitness`); it is split in two (this one and g6-art20-court-orders) because the two Articles are
-- separately citable, one module would run to about a thousand lines, and neither needs the other's rules: Article 19 refers to Article 20 only as a source of a
-- permission (data here) and an application to the court (a fact here).
-- Inputs from other groups (PLAN section (c)): IP5 `the entity` and IP6 `the entity is a registered charity` (G1), IP19 `the required steps notices served` (G8),
-- IP20 (the organized-religious flag, a field of `the registered charity`, G8), IP12 as a field of the governor's conduct record (G1).
-- Outputs: IP21 `Art 19(1) the reportable matters of the person` (the kinds of reportable matter), IP22 `the applicant has complied with Article 19(5)`,
-- IP23 `Article 19(9)(c) bars granting the application`, IP30 `the penalty provided for the offence` (Article 19(11)).
-- A discretion is an input: "promptly", "reasonable excuse", "fit and proper person", "necessary" and "reasonable time" are determinations the caller supplies.
-- Dates are DATEs; the day on which a status is asked is a GIVEN, `the day in question`.

§ `Part 5 -- Governors of registered charities`

§§ `Article 19 -- Reportable matters and acting as a governor`

-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The nouns of this Article (group-local; the integrator may move any of them to domain.l4, see FRAGMENT-G6.md section (4))
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- What a person does under Article 19, value-actor style: the first actor field of each act is its performer.
DECLARE `Act under Article 19` IS ONE OF
    `report the reportable matter to the entity or charity` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `report the reportable matter to the Commissioner` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `provide a declaration that there is no reportable matter` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `state that the entity holds declarations from all its governors who have not made a report` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `explain to the Commissioner the reason for contravening paragraph (5)` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `act as a governor of a registered charity` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `make inquiries to determine whether the governor is a fit and proper person` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `apply to the court to determine whether the governor is a fit and proper person` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `grant the application for registration` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `permit the governor to act as a governor until the issue is determined or the notice is withdrawn` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `notify the entity that the application will be refused unless the governor is removed` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `serve a required steps notice requiring the charity to suspend or remove the governor` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `give permission for the governor to act as a governor by notice entered in the register` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `prescribe by Order a description of reportable matter` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`

-- A disqualification (or an equivalent restriction) under the law of the United Kingdom or of another jurisdiction (Article 19(1)(c) and (d)).
DECLARE `Disqualification elsewhere` HAS
    `imposed on` IS A DATE
        @desc The day the disqualification was imposed
    `last day in force` IS A MAYBE DATE
        @desc The last day on which the disqualification applies; NOTHING while it has no end

-- A conviction of the person. Whether it is spent is decided by another Law (the rehabilitation of offenders), so it is a fact per conviction.
DECLARE `Conviction of a person` HAS
    `for an offence under this Law` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the offence is one under the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014
    `for an offence falling within Article 2(10)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the offence falls within Article 2(10)(b)
    spent IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the conviction is spent

-- The raw facts about one person from which Article 19(1) names the reportable matters. The conduct fields are those Article 18(4) reads for the misconduct of (a).
DECLARE `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` HAS
    `conduct as a governor` IS A `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)`
        @desc This person's conduct as a governor of the registered charity, as Article 18(4) reads it
    `the governors of the charity` IS A LIST OF `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)`
        @desc The conduct of every governor of the charity, this person included
    `the conduct of the charity is misconduct within Article 2(10)` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the charity's own conduct is misconduct within Article 2(10)
    `the misconduct led to the service of a required steps notice` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether this person's misconduct as a governor led to the service of a required steps notice on that governor, on the charity or on another governor
    `disqualification orders under this Law` IS A LIST OF `Disqualification order`
        @desc The disqualification orders under this Law made against this person
    `subject to another restriction on acting as a governor under this Law` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the person is subject to any other restriction on acting as a governor imposed under this Law
    `disqualifications as a charity trustee or an equivalent` IS A LIST OF `Disqualification elsewhere`
        @desc Disqualifications from being a charity trustee under the law of any part of the United Kingdom, or from an equivalent position under the law of any other jurisdiction
    `disqualifications as a company director or an equivalent outside Jersey` IS A LIST OF `Disqualification elsewhere`
        @desc Disqualifications from being a company director, or an equivalent disqualification under the law of a jurisdiction other than Jersey
    `bankrupt or otherwise insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the person is bankrupt or otherwise insolvent, under the law of Jersey or elsewhere
    convictions IS A LIST OF `Conviction of a person`
        @desc The person's convictions
    `falls within another description prescribed by Order` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the person falls within a description the Minister has prescribed by Order under Article 19(1)(h)

§§§ `Article 19(1) -- the reportable matters`

-- src:484 | (a) has engaged in misconduct as a governor of a registered charity, being misconduct that led to the service of a required steps notice on that governor or on that charity or on another governor of that charity;
@ref Article 19(1)(a) (src:484)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      `the required steps notices served` IS A LIST OF `Required steps notice`
      person IS A `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 19(1)(a) the person has engaged in misconduct as a governor that led to a required steps notice` interp `the required steps notices served` person MEANS
        `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` interp (person's `the conduct of the charity is misconduct within Article 2(10)`) (person's `the governors of the charity`) (person's `conduct as a governor`)
    AND person's `the misconduct led to the service of a required steps notice`
    AND NOT null `the required steps notices served`

-- src:485 | (b) is the subject of a disqualification order, or of any other restriction on his or her acting as a governor, imposed under this Law;
@ref Article 19(1)(b) (src:485)
GIVEN `the day in question` IS A DATE
      person IS A `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 19(1)(b) the person is the subject of a disqualification order or another restriction` `the day in question` person MEANS
        any (GIVEN order YIELD
                    order's person EQUALS person's `conduct as a governor`'s name
                AND `the disqualification order is in force on the day` order `the day in question`)
            (person's `disqualification orders under this Law`)
    OR  person's `subject to another restriction on acting as a governor under this Law`

@ref Article 19(1)(c) and (d) (src:486-487)
GIVEN item IS A `Disqualification elsewhere`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the disqualification elsewhere is in force on the day` item day MEANS
        item's `imposed on` AT MOST day
    AND CONSIDER item's `last day in force`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST last THEN day AT MOST last

-- F6.9: "has been disqualified". The present perfect says the person has been disqualified; it does not say the disqualification must still bind (contrast (f), "whether or not spent",
-- and (g), "unspent", which say expressly how far back or forward they reach). The reading taken counts any disqualification already imposed on the day in question.
@ref Article 19(1)(c) and (d) (F6.9) (src:486-487)
GIVEN `the day in question` IS A DATE
      items IS A LIST OF `Disqualification elsewhere`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F6.9 reading A: a disqualification counts although it has ended` `the day in question` items MEANS
    any (GIVEN item YIELD item's `imposed on` AT MOST `the day in question`) items

@ref Article 19(1)(c) and (d) (F6.9) (src:486-487)
GIVEN `the day in question` IS A DATE
      items IS A LIST OF `Disqualification elsewhere`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F6.9 reading B: only a disqualification still in force counts` `the day in question` items MEANS
    any (GIVEN item YIELD `the disqualification elsewhere is in force on the day` item `the day in question`) items

@ref Article 19(1)(c) and (d) (F6.9) (src:486-487)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
      items IS A LIST OF `Disqualification elsewhere`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a disqualification elsewhere is a reportable matter` interp `the day in question` items MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `whether a disqualification that has ended is a reportable matter`
    WHEN `a disqualification counts although it has ended`
        THEN `F6.9 reading A: a disqualification counts although it has ended` `the day in question` items
    WHEN `only a disqualification still in force counts`
        THEN `F6.9 reading B: only a disqualification still in force counts` `the day in question` items

-- src:486 | (c) has been disqualified from or for being a charity trustee or trustee for a charity under the law of any part of the United Kingdom, or from holding any equivalent position under the law of any other jurisdiction;
@ref Article 19(1)(c) (src:486)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
      person IS A `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 19(1)(c) the person has been disqualified as a charity trustee or from an equivalent position` interp `the day in question` person MEANS
    `a disqualification elsewhere is a reportable matter` interp `the day in question` (person's `disqualifications as a charity trustee or an equivalent`)

-- src:487 | (d) has been disqualified from being a company director, or has been made subject to any equivalent disqualification under the law of any jurisdiction other than Jersey;
@ref Article 19(1)(d) (src:487)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
      person IS A `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 19(1)(d) the person has been disqualified as a company director or from an equivalent position` interp `the day in question` person MEANS
    `a disqualification elsewhere is a reportable matter` interp `the day in question` (person's `disqualifications as a company director or an equivalent outside Jersey`)

-- Endnote [3] (src:937): in sub-paragraph (e) "law or Jersey" was replaced by "law of Jersey" (an editorial change); the text read here is the text as it now stands.
-- src:488 | (e) is bankrupt or otherwise insolvent, whether under the law of Jersey or elsewhere;
@ref Article 19(1)(e) (src:488)
GIVEN person IS A `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 19(1)(e) the person is bankrupt or otherwise insolvent` person MEANS
    person's `bankrupt or otherwise insolvent`

-- src:489 | (f) has a conviction (whether or not spent) for an offence under this Law;
@ref Article 19(1)(f) (src:489)
GIVEN person IS A `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 19(1)(f) the person has a conviction, spent or not, for an offence under this Law` person MEANS
    any (GIVEN conviction YIELD conviction's `for an offence under this Law`) (person's convictions)

-- src:490 | (g) has an unspent conviction for an offence falling within Article 2(10)(b); or
@ref Article 19(1)(g) (src:490)
GIVEN person IS A `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 19(1)(g) the person has an unspent conviction for an offence falling within Article 2(10)(b)` person MEANS
    any (GIVEN conviction YIELD
                conviction's `for an offence falling within Article 2(10)(b)`
            AND NOT conviction's spent)
        (person's convictions)

-- src:491 | (h) falls within any other description that may be prescribed by the Minister by Order.[3]
@ref Article 19(1)(h) (src:491)
GIVEN person IS A `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 19(1)(h) the person falls within another description prescribed by Order` person MEANS
    person's `falls within another description prescribed by Order`

-- The power behind (h): the Minister may prescribe a further description by Order. What the Order says is an input (the caller's `falls within another description prescribed by Order`).
-- src:491 | (h) falls within any other description that may be prescribed by the Minister by Order.[3]
@ref Article 19(1)(h) (src:491)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 19`
`Art 19(1)(h) the Minister may prescribe a further description of reportable matter by Order` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY   `prescribe by Order a description of reportable matter` `the Minister`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:483 | (1) A reportable matter in relation to a person is the fact that the person –
-- src:484 | (a) has engaged in misconduct as a governor of a registered charity, being misconduct that led to the service of a required steps notice on that governor or on that charity or on another governor of that charity;
-- src:485 | (b) is the subject of a disqualification order, or of any other restriction on his or her acting as a governor, imposed under this Law;
-- src:486 | (c) has been disqualified from or for being a charity trustee or trustee for a charity under the law of any part of the United Kingdom, or from holding any equivalent position under the law of any other jurisdiction;
-- src:487 | (d) has been disqualified from being a company director, or has been made subject to any equivalent disqualification under the law of any jurisdiction other than Jersey;
-- src:488 | (e) is bankrupt or otherwise insolvent, whether under the law of Jersey or elsewhere;
-- src:489 | (f) has a conviction (whether or not spent) for an offence under this Law;
-- src:490 | (g) has an unspent conviction for an offence falling within Article 2(10)(b); or
-- src:491 | (h) falls within any other description that may be prescribed by the Minister by Order.[3]
@ref Article 19(1) (src:483-491)
@export Which of the eight descriptions of Article 19(1) apply to a person on a day, as a list of kinds of reportable matter (empty if none); the answer is IP21 and fills the field reportable matters of the governor
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
        @desc The readings of the open points of Articles 15 to 20; here F6.9 (whether a disqualification that has ended is a reportable matter)
      `the required steps notices served` IS A LIST OF `Required steps notice`
        @desc The required steps notices served on the charity or its governors (IP19)
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
        @desc The day on which the reportable matters are asked
      person IS A `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)`
        @desc The facts about the person
GIVETH A LIST OF `Kind of reportable matter`
`Art 19(1) the reportable matters of the person` interp `the required steps notices served` `the day in question` person MEANS
    mapMaybe (GIVEN pair YIELD IF pair's snd THEN JUST (pair's fst) ELSE NOTHING)
        (LIST (PAIR OF `misconduct as a governor that led to a required steps notice`, `Art 19(1)(a) the person has engaged in misconduct as a governor that led to a required steps notice` interp `the required steps notices served` person)
            , (PAIR OF `a disqualification order or other restriction on acting as a governor imposed under this Law`, `Art 19(1)(b) the person is the subject of a disqualification order or another restriction` `the day in question` person)
            , (PAIR OF `disqualification as a charity trustee under the law of the United Kingdom or an equivalent position elsewhere`, `Art 19(1)(c) the person has been disqualified as a charity trustee or from an equivalent position` interp `the day in question` person)
            , (PAIR OF `disqualification as a company director, or an equivalent disqualification outside Jersey`, `Art 19(1)(d) the person has been disqualified as a company director or from an equivalent position` interp `the day in question` person)
            , (PAIR OF `bankruptcy or other insolvency`, `Art 19(1)(e) the person is bankrupt or otherwise insolvent` person)
            , (PAIR OF `a conviction, whether or not spent, for an offence under this Law`, `Art 19(1)(f) the person has a conviction, spent or not, for an offence under this Law` person)
            , (PAIR OF `an unspent conviction for an offence falling within Article 2(10)(b)`, `Art 19(1)(g) the person has an unspent conviction for an offence falling within Article 2(10)(b)` person)
            , (PAIR OF `a description prescribed by Order`, `Art 19(1)(h) the person falls within another description prescribed by Order` person))

§§§ `Article 19(2) -- the duty to report a reportable matter`

-- An entity "applying for registration" is the standing `an applicant for registration`.
@ref Article 19(2) and (3) (src:492) (src:493)
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the entity is an applicant for registration` `the entity` MEANS
    `the entity`'s `standing on the register` EQUALS `an applicant for registration`

-- Where the Law gives no number of days for "promptly", the readings that need one have none to use.
@ref Article 19(2) (src:492)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Art 19(2) the Law gives no number of days that count as prompt` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 19(2) says that a report must be made promptly and gives no number of days, so a reading that counts days has nothing to count with unless the caller supplies the number"

-- What the caller knows about one governor's reports of the reportable matters. The dates are those of the earliest matter and of the reports that covered the matters.
DECLARE `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)` HAS
    `the matter arose on` IS A DATE
        @desc The day the reportable matter arose
    `the governor became aware of the matter on` IS A DATE
        @desc The day the governor became aware of the matter
    `reported to the entity or charity on` IS A MAYBE DATE
        @desc The day the governor reported to the entity or the charity; NOTHING if not yet
    `reported to the Commissioner on` IS A MAYBE DATE
        @desc The day the governor reported to the Commissioner; NOTHING if not yet
    `the reports were made promptly` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the governor's reports were prompt, as a determination (read under the reading that promptness is supplied as an input)
    `a prompt time has run out` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether, on the day in question, the time within which a prompt report should have been made has run out (read under the same reading)

-- F6.12. The Law says "promptly" and gives no number. The reading taken treats promptness as a determination the caller supplies, like "reasonable" and "satisfied" elsewhere.
-- The other two readings count days, from the matter arising or from the governor becoming aware, against a number the caller supplies.
@ref Article 19(2) (F6.12) (src:492)
GIVEN `the longest interval that counts as prompt, in days` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days that count as prompt` `the longest interval that counts as prompt, in days` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the longest interval that counts as prompt, in days`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `Art 19(2) the Law gives no number of days that count as prompt`
    WHEN JUST n THEN n

@ref Article 19(2) (F6.12) (src:492)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      `the longest interval that counts as prompt, in days` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      position IS A `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)`
      report IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 19(2) the report made on the date is prompt` interp `the longest interval that counts as prompt, in days` position report MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `how a report is judged prompt under Article 19(2)`
    WHEN `promptness is a determination supplied as an input`
        THEN position's `the reports were made promptly`
    WHEN `promptness is a number of days from the matter arising`
        THEN (Day report MINUS Day (position's `the matter arose on`)) AT MOST `the number of days that count as prompt` `the longest interval that counts as prompt, in days`
    WHEN `promptness is a number of days from the governor becoming aware of the matter`
        THEN (Day report MINUS Day (position's `the governor became aware of the matter on`)) AT MOST `the number of days that count as prompt` `the longest interval that counts as prompt, in days`

@ref Article 19(2) (F6.12) (src:492)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      `the longest interval that counts as prompt, in days` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      position IS A `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)`
      made IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 19(2) the report made on the optional date is prompt` interp `the longest interval that counts as prompt, in days` position made MEANS
    CONSIDER made
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST report THEN `Art 19(2) the report made on the date is prompt` interp `the longest interval that counts as prompt, in days` position report

-- The governor has complied with paragraph (2) when both reports have been made, and made promptly.
-- src:492 | (2) A governor of an entity applying for registration, or of a registered charity, must report any reportable matter promptly to that entity or charity and to the Commissioner.
@ref Article 19(2) (src:492)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      `the longest interval that counts as prompt, in days` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      position IS A `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 19(2) the governor has complied with paragraph (2)` interp `the longest interval that counts as prompt, in days` position MEANS
        `Art 19(2) the report made on the optional date is prompt` interp `the longest interval that counts as prompt, in days` position (position's `reported to the entity or charity on`)
    AND `Art 19(2) the report made on the optional date is prompt` interp `the longest interval that counts as prompt, in days` position (position's `reported to the Commissioner on`)

@ref Article 19(2), (3) and (4) (src:492) (src:493) (src:494)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      made IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the report had been made by the day` day made MEANS
    CONSIDER made
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST report THEN report AT MOST day

-- A governor is in breach of paragraph (2) on a day while the matter is unreported and the time for a prompt report has run out. The reading taken is that a governor who has made both reports is
-- no longer in breach on later days (the duty is to report, and it has been done); the late report was a breach when it was due, and Article 19(10) bars the governor from then on.
-- Under the counting readings, the report is due within N days: the last prompt day is the anchor day plus N, and the governor is in breach from the day after it.
@ref Article 19(2) (F6.12) (src:492)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      `the longest interval that counts as prompt, in days` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
      position IS A `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the time for a prompt report has run out` interp `the longest interval that counts as prompt, in days` `the day in question` position MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `how a report is judged prompt under Article 19(2)`
    WHEN `promptness is a determination supplied as an input`
        THEN position's `a prompt time has run out`
    WHEN `promptness is a number of days from the matter arising`
        THEN (Day `the day in question` MINUS Day (position's `the matter arose on`)) GREATER THAN `the number of days that count as prompt` `the longest interval that counts as prompt, in days`
    WHEN `promptness is a number of days from the governor becoming aware of the matter`
        THEN (Day `the day in question` MINUS Day (position's `the governor became aware of the matter on`)) GREATER THAN `the number of days that count as prompt` `the longest interval that counts as prompt, in days`

-- src:492 | (2) A governor of an entity applying for registration, or of a registered charity, must report any reportable matter promptly to that entity or charity and to the Commissioner.
@ref Article 19(2) (src:492)
@export Whether a governor who has a reportable matter is in breach of the duty to report it promptly on a given day (the matter is unreported to the entity or charity or to the Commissioner, and the time for a prompt report has run out); a governor with no reportable matter is never in breach
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
        @desc The readings of the open points of Articles 15 to 20; here F6.12 (how promptness is judged)
      `the longest interval that counts as prompt, in days` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
        @desc The number of days that count as prompt, if the reading that counts days is chosen; NOTHING if the Law's silence is to be respected
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
        @desc The day on which the breach is asked
      `the governor` IS A Governor
        @desc The governor, with the reportable matters that describe them
      position IS A `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)`
        @desc What the governor has reported, and when
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 19(2) the governor is in breach of paragraph (2)` interp `the longest interval that counts as prompt, in days` `the day in question` `the governor` position MEANS
        NOT null (`the governor`'s `reportable matters`)
    AND NOT (    `the report had been made by the day` `the day in question` (position's `reported to the entity or charity on`)
             AND `the report had been made by the day` `the day in question` (position's `reported to the Commissioner on`))
    AND `the time for a prompt report has run out` interp `the longest interval that counts as prompt, in days` `the day in question` position

-- The duty itself: a governor of an entity applying for registration, or of a registered charity, must report any reportable matter to that entity or charity and to the Commissioner.
-- The duty states no period (promptness is judged by the functions above), so the rule carries no WITHIN.
-- src:492 | (2) A governor of an entity applying for registration, or of a registered charity, must report any reportable matter promptly to that entity or charity and to the Commissioner.
@ref Article 19(2) (src:492)
@export Whether and how a governor of an entity applying for registration or of a registered charity must report a reportable matter to the entity or charity and to the Commissioner; nothing is owed where the governor has no reportable matter
GIVEN `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the entity is entered in the general or the restricted section of the register
      `the entity` IS AN Entity
        @desc The entity, with its standing on the register
      `the governor` IS A Governor
        @desc The governor, with the reportable matters that describe them
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 19`
`Art 19(2) the governor must report the reportable matter` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity` `the governor` MEANS
    IF       (   `the entity is a registered charity`
              OR `the entity is an applicant for registration` `the entity`)
         AND NOT null (`the governor`'s `reportable matters`)
    THEN     (PARTY `a governor`
              MUST  `report the reportable matter to the entity or charity` `a governor`
              HENCE FULFILLED)
        RAND (PARTY `a governor`
              MUST  `report the reportable matter to the Commissioner` `a governor`
              HENCE FULFILLED)
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§§ `Article 19(3) -- the declaration by a governor of an entity applying for registration`

-- F6.20: "before the application is made". A date has no hour in it, so a declaration given on the day of the application cannot be placed before or after it.
-- The reading taken counts the day of the application as in time (the declaration was given before the application was made, on that day); the other requires an earlier day.
@ref Article 19(3) (F6.20) (src:493)
GIVEN provided IS A MAYBE DATE
      application IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F6.20 reading A: a declaration given on the day of the application is in time` provided application MEANS
    CONSIDER provided
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST d THEN d AT MOST application

@ref Article 19(3) (F6.20) (src:493)
GIVEN provided IS A MAYBE DATE
      application IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F6.20 reading B: a declaration must be given on an earlier day than the application` provided application MEANS
    CONSIDER provided
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST d THEN d LESS THAN application

-- src:493 | (3) A governor of an entity applying for registration must, if there is no reportable matter in relation to that governor, provide to the entity a declaration to that effect before the application is made.
@ref Article 19(3) (src:493)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      provided IS A MAYBE DATE
      application IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 19(3) the declaration was provided before the application was made` interp provided application MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `whether a declaration given on the day of the application is in time`
    WHEN `a declaration given on the day of the application is in time`
        THEN `F6.20 reading A: a declaration given on the day of the application is in time` provided application
    WHEN `a declaration must be given on an earlier day than the application`
        THEN `F6.20 reading B: a declaration must be given on an earlier day than the application` provided application

-- The closing day of the duty, on each reading: the day of the application, or the day before it.
@ref Article 19(3) (F6.20) (src:493)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      application IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the declaration of Article 19(3)` interp application MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `whether a declaration given on the day of the application is in time`
    WHEN `a declaration given on the day of the application is in time` THEN application
    WHEN `a declaration must be given on an earlier day than the application` THEN `the day before` application

-- src:493 | (3) A governor of an entity applying for registration must, if there is no reportable matter in relation to that governor, provide to the entity a declaration to that effect before the application is made.
@ref Article 19(3) (src:493)
@export Whether and how a governor of an entity applying for registration, who has no reportable matter, must provide the entity with a declaration to that effect before the application is made; nothing is owed where the entity is not applying or the governor has a reportable matter
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
        @desc The readings of the open points of Articles 15 to 20; here F6.20 (whether a declaration given on the day of the application is in time)
      `the entity` IS AN Entity
        @desc The entity, with its standing on the register
      `the governor` IS A Governor
        @desc The governor, with the reportable matters that describe them
      application IS A DATE
        @desc The day the application for registration is made
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 19`
`Art 19(3) the governor of an applicant must provide a declaration of no reportable matter` interp `the entity` `the governor` application MEANS
    IF       `the entity is an applicant for registration` `the entity`
         AND null (`the governor`'s `reportable matters`)
    THEN PARTY  `a governor`
         MUST   `provide a declaration that there is no reportable matter` `a governor`
         BEFORE `the last day for the declaration of Article 19(3)` interp application
         HENCE  FULFILLED
         LEST   BREACH BY `a governor` BECAUSE "Article 19(3): the declaration that there is no reportable matter was not provided to the entity before the application was made"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§§ `Article 19(4) -- the declaration by a governor of a registered charity`

DECLARE `Position of a governor under Article 19(4)` HAS
    `notified by the charity on` IS A MAYBE DATE
        @desc The day the charity notified the governor that it is preparing its annual return; NOTHING if not yet notified
    `declaration provided on` IS A MAYBE DATE
        @desc The day the governor provided the charity with the declaration; NOTHING if not yet
    `a reasonable time has passed since the notification` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether, on the day in question, a reasonable time has passed since the notification (read only under the reading that allows a reasonable time)

-- F6.21: "when notified". The duty is to provide the declaration "when notified by the charity that it is preparing its annual return": the Law states no period after the notification.
-- The reading taken is that the declaration is due on the day of the notification, so the governor is in breach from the next day; the other allows a reasonable time (a determination the caller supplies).
@ref Article 19(4) (F6.21) (src:494)
GIVEN notified IS A MAYBE DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the notification was given before the day` notified day MEANS
    CONSIDER notified
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST given THEN given LESS THAN day

@ref Article 19(4) (F6.21) (src:494)
GIVEN notified IS A MAYBE DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the notification was given by the day` notified day MEANS
    CONSIDER notified
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST given THEN given AT MOST day

@ref Article 19(4) (F6.21) (src:494)
GIVEN `the day in question` IS A DATE
      position IS A `Position of a governor under Article 19(4)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F6.21 reading A: the governor is in breach from the day after the notification` `the day in question` position MEANS
        `the notification was given before the day` (position's `notified by the charity on`) `the day in question`
    AND NOT `the report had been made by the day` `the day in question` (position's `declaration provided on`)

@ref Article 19(4) (F6.21) (src:494)
GIVEN `the day in question` IS A DATE
      position IS A `Position of a governor under Article 19(4)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F6.21 reading B: the governor is in breach once a reasonable time has passed after the notification` `the day in question` position MEANS
        `the notification was given by the day` (position's `notified by the charity on`) `the day in question`
    AND position's `a reasonable time has passed since the notification`
    AND NOT `the report had been made by the day` `the day in question` (position's `declaration provided on`)

@ref Article 19(4) (F6.21) (src:494)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
      position IS A `Position of a governor under Article 19(4)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the governor who has been notified is in breach of paragraph (4)` interp `the day in question` position MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `from when a governor who has been notified is in breach of Article 19(4)`
    WHEN `the governor is in breach from the day after the notification`
        THEN `F6.21 reading A: the governor is in breach from the day after the notification` `the day in question` position
    WHEN `the governor is in breach once a reasonable time has passed after the notification`
        THEN `F6.21 reading B: the governor is in breach once a reasonable time has passed after the notification` `the day in question` position

-- src:494 | (4) A governor of a registered charity must, if there is no reportable matter in relation to that governor, provide to the charity a declaration to that effect when notified by the charity that it is preparing its annual return.
@ref Article 19(4) (src:494)
@export Whether a governor of a registered charity who has no reportable matter is in breach of the duty to provide the charity with a declaration to that effect when notified that it is preparing its annual return, on a given day
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
        @desc The readings of the open points of Articles 15 to 20; here F6.21 (from when a notified governor is in breach)
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the entity is entered in the general or the restricted section of the register
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
        @desc The day on which the breach is asked
      `the governor` IS A Governor
        @desc The governor, with the reportable matters that describe them
      position IS A `Position of a governor under Article 19(4)`
        @desc When the charity notified the governor and when the governor provided the declaration
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 19(4) the governor is in breach of paragraph (4)` interp `the entity is a registered charity` `the day in question` `the governor` position MEANS
        `the entity is a registered charity`
    AND null (`the governor`'s `reportable matters`)
    AND `the governor who has been notified is in breach of paragraph (4)` interp `the day in question` position

-- The duty arises on the notification. On the reading taken it falls due the same day (WITHIN 0 on a trace that starts at the notification); on the other it is a standing duty.
@ref Article 19(4) (F6.21) (src:494)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 19`
`F6.21 reading A: the declaration is due on the day of the notification` MEANS
    PARTY  `a governor`
    MUST   `provide a declaration that there is no reportable matter` `a governor`
    WITHIN 0
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `a governor` BECAUSE "Article 19(4): the declaration that there is no reportable matter was not provided to the charity on the day it notified the governor that it is preparing its annual return"

@ref Article 19(4) (F6.21) (src:494)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 19`
`F6.21 reading B: the declaration is due within a reasonable time after the notification` MEANS
    PARTY  `a governor`
    MUST   `provide a declaration that there is no reportable matter` `a governor`
    HENCE  FULFILLED

-- src:494 | (4) A governor of a registered charity must, if there is no reportable matter in relation to that governor, provide to the charity a declaration to that effect when notified by the charity that it is preparing its annual return.
@ref Article 19(4) (src:494)
@export Whether and how a governor of a registered charity, who has no reportable matter and has been notified that the charity is preparing its annual return, must provide the charity with a declaration to that effect; nothing is owed before the notification, where the governor has a reportable matter, or where the entity is not a registered charity (run a trace from the day of the notification)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
        @desc The readings of the open points of Articles 15 to 20; here F6.21
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the entity is entered in the general or the restricted section of the register
      `the governor` IS A Governor
        @desc The governor, with the reportable matters that describe them
      `the charity has notified the governor` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the charity has notified the governor that it is preparing its annual return
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 19`
`Art 19(4) the governor of a registered charity must provide a declaration of no reportable matter` interp `the entity is a registered charity` `the governor` `the charity has notified the governor` MEANS
    IF       `the entity is a registered charity`
         AND null (`the governor`'s `reportable matters`)
         AND `the charity has notified the governor`
    THEN CONSIDER interp's `from when a governor who has been notified is in breach of Article 19(4)`
         WHEN `the governor is in breach from the day after the notification`
            THEN `F6.21 reading A: the declaration is due on the day of the notification`
         WHEN `the governor is in breach once a reasonable time has passed after the notification`
            THEN `F6.21 reading B: the declaration is due within a reasonable time after the notification`
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§§ `Article 19(5), (6) and (7) -- the statement that declarations are held`

-- One governor's position for the statement. A governor who has made a report under paragraph (2) is not counted; every other governor must have given a declaration.
DECLARE `Position of a governor for Article 19(5)` HAS
    name IS A STRING
        @desc The governor's name
    `made a report under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the governor has made a report of a reportable matter under Article 19(2)
    `provided a declaration of no reportable matter` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the governor has provided a declaration under Article 19(3) or (4)

-- "That it has declarations from all of its governors who have not made a report under paragraph (2)": the statement is true when every governor either has reported or has declared.
@ref Article 19(5) (src:495)
GIVEN governors IS A LIST OF `Position of a governor for Article 19(5)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 19(5) the entity holds declarations from all its governors who have not made a report` governors MEANS
    all (GIVEN position YIELD
                position's `made a report under paragraph (2)`
            OR  position's `provided a declaration of no reportable matter`)
        governors

-- The duty is to state it, and to state it truly: complying means making the statement AND having the declarations the statement says are held.
-- src:495 | (5) The entity must state in its application, and the registered charity must state in its annual return, that it has declarations from all of its governors who have not made a report under paragraph (2).
@ref Article 19(5) (src:495)
@export Whether an entity applying for registration has complied with Article 19(5): its application states that it holds declarations from all its governors who have not made a report, and it does hold them; the answer is IP22
GIVEN `the application states that the entity holds declarations from all its governors who have not made a report` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the application contains the statement
      governors IS A LIST OF `Position of a governor for Article 19(5)`
        @desc One position for each governor of the applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 19(5) the applicant has stated that it holds declarations from all its governors who have not reported` `the application states that the entity holds declarations from all its governors who have not made a report` governors MEANS
        `the application states that the entity holds declarations from all its governors who have not made a report`
    AND `Art 19(5) the entity holds declarations from all its governors who have not made a report` governors

-- src:495 | (5) The entity must state in its application, and the registered charity must state in its annual return, that it has declarations from all of its governors who have not made a report under paragraph (2).
@ref Article 19(5) (src:495)
@export Whether a registered charity has complied with Article 19(5) in its annual return: the return states that it holds declarations from all its governors who have not made a report, and it does hold them
GIVEN `the annual return states that the charity holds declarations from all its governors who have not made a report` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the annual return contains the statement
      governors IS A LIST OF `Position of a governor for Article 19(5)`
        @desc One position for each governor of the registered charity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 19(5) the registered charity has stated in its annual return that it holds declarations` `the annual return states that the charity holds declarations from all its governors who have not made a report` governors MEANS
        `the annual return states that the charity holds declarations from all its governors who have not made a report`
    AND `Art 19(5) the entity holds declarations from all its governors who have not made a report` governors

-- The duty of paragraph (5), as two obligations of two parties: the applicant in its application, the registered charity in its annual return. Neither states a period.
-- src:495 | (5) The entity must state in its application, and the registered charity must state in its annual return, that it has declarations from all of its governors who have not made a report under paragraph (2).
@ref Article 19(5) (src:495)
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 19`
`Art 19(5) the entity must state that it holds declarations` `the entity` MEANS
    IF   `the entity is an applicant for registration` `the entity`
    THEN PARTY `an applicant for registration`
         MUST  `state that the entity holds declarations from all its governors who have not made a report` `an applicant for registration`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `a registered charity`
         MUST  `state that the entity holds declarations from all its governors who have not made a report` `a registered charity`
         HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:496 | (6) An application for registration is not complete if the entity has not complied with paragraph (5).
@ref Article 19(6) (src:496)
@export Whether an application for registration is incomplete for want of the statement of Article 19(5) (it is not complete if the entity has not complied with paragraph (5))
GIVEN `the applicant has complied with Article 19(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the applicant has complied with Article 19(5) (IP22)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 19(6) the application is not complete for want of Article 19(5)` `the applicant has complied with Article 19(5)` MEANS
    NOT `the applicant has complied with Article 19(5)`

-- src:497 | (7) A registered charity that contravenes paragraph (5) must explain to the Commissioner the reason for the contravention.
@ref Article 19(7) (src:497)
@export Whether and how a registered charity that has contravened paragraph (5) must explain the reason to the Commissioner; nothing is owed if it complied
GIVEN `the registered charity has complied with Article 19(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the registered charity has complied with Article 19(5) in its annual return
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 19`
`Art 19(7) the registered charity that contravenes paragraph (5) must explain the reason to the Commissioner` `the registered charity has complied with Article 19(5)` MEANS
    IF   `the registered charity has complied with Article 19(5)`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `a registered charity`
         MUST  `explain to the Commissioner the reason for contravening paragraph (5)` `a registered charity`
         HENCE FULFILLED

§§§ `Article 19(8) -- the bar on acting while in breach of paragraph (2) or (4)`

-- No offence attaches to a contravention of paragraph (8) on the reading taken (F6.11): Article 19(11) names only paragraph (10). The prohibition is therefore a SHANT whose breach carries no penalty;
-- the penalty a reader might expect is a separate function so that the other reading is callable.
-- src:498 | (8) A person must not act as a governor of a registered charity at any time when the person is in breach of paragraph (2) or (4).
@ref Article 19(8) (src:498)
@export Whether a person must not act as a governor of a registered charity on a day on which the person is in breach of Article 19(2) or (4); the prohibition carries no penalty on the reading taken (see the penalty function)
GIVEN `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the entity is entered in the general or the restricted section of the register
      `the person is in breach of paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the person is in breach of Article 19(2) on the day in question
      `the person is in breach of paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the person is in breach of Article 19(4) on the day in question
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 19`
`Art 19(8) the person must not act as a governor while in breach of Article 19(2) or (4)` `the entity is a registered charity` `the person is in breach of paragraph (2)` `the person is in breach of paragraph (4)` MEANS
    IF       `the entity is a registered charity`
         AND (   `the person is in breach of paragraph (2)`
              OR `the person is in breach of paragraph (4)`)
    THEN PARTY `any person`
         SHANT `act as a governor of a registered charity` `any person`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `any person` BECAUSE "Article 19(8): acted as a governor of a registered charity while in breach of Article 19(2) or (4); no offence is attached to paragraph (8) on the reading taken"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- The penalty for a contravention of paragraph (8): none on the reading taken; the penalty of paragraph (11) on the other (F6.11).
@ref Article 19(8) and (11) (F6.11) (src:498) (src:510)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
GIVETH A `Penalty provided`
`Art 19(8) the penalty for contravening Article 19(8)` interp MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `whether acting in breach of Article 19(2) or (4) is an offence`
    WHEN `Article 19(11) reaches only paragraph (10)`
        THEN `Penalty provided` WITH
                 `imprisonment up to, in months` IS NOTHING
                 fine IS `no fine is provided`
    WHEN `Article 19(11) reaches paragraph (8) as well`
        THEN `Art 19(11) the penalty for contravening Article 19(10)`

§§§ `Article 19(9) -- what the Commissioner does when a governor reports a reportable matter to the Commissioner`

-- What the caller knows about one report of a reportable matter to the Commissioner. "Determined" and "resulting order or notice" are facts; whether the governor is fit and proper is the Commissioner's
-- or the court's determination and is not modelled.
DECLARE `Reported matter under Article 19(9)` HAS
    `the governor reported the matter to the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the governor reported the reportable matter to the Commissioner
    `the Commissioner has applied to the court to determine the issue` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the Commissioner has applied to the court under Article 19(9)(b) (or Article 19(13)), so that the issue is to be determined by the court
    `the issue has been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the issue whether the governor is a fit and proper person has been determined
    `any resulting order or notice has been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether any order or notice resulting from the determination has been complied with; TRUE where none resulted

-- src:499 | (9) If a governor reports a reportable matter to the Commissioner, the Commissioner –
-- src:500 | (a) must make inquiries to determine whether the governor is a fit and proper person to be a governor;
@ref Article 19(9)(a) (src:499-500)
@export Whether and how the Commissioner must make inquiries to determine whether a governor who has reported a reportable matter to the Commissioner is a fit and proper person; no deadline is stated
GIVEN reported IS A `Reported matter under Article 19(9)`
        @desc The report of the reportable matter to the Commissioner
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 19`
`Art 19(9)(a) the Commissioner must make inquiries into whether the governor is a fit and proper person` reported MEANS
    IF   reported's `the governor reported the matter to the Commissioner`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MUST  `make inquiries to determine whether the governor is a fit and proper person` `the Commissioner`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:499 | (9) If a governor reports a reportable matter to the Commissioner, the Commissioner –
-- src:501 | (b) may apply to the court to determine that issue under Article 20;
@ref Article 19(9)(b) (src:499) (src:501)
@export Whether the Commissioner may apply to the court to determine whether a governor who has reported a reportable matter is a fit and proper person
GIVEN reported IS A `Reported matter under Article 19(9)`
        @desc The report of the reportable matter to the Commissioner
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 19`
`Art 19(9)(b) the Commissioner may apply to the court to determine the issue` reported MEANS
    IF   reported's `the governor reported the matter to the Commissioner`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MAY   `apply to the court to determine whether the governor is a fit and proper person` `the Commissioner`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (c): for an application for registration, the application may not be granted until the issue is determined and any resulting order or notice complied with. IP23 is the BOOLEAN:
-- some governor has reported to the Commissioner and either the issue is undetermined or the resulting order or notice has not been complied with.
-- src:502 | (c) must not, in the case of an application for registration, grant that application until the issue has been determined and any resulting order or notice complied with;
@ref Article 19(9)(c) (src:502)
@export Whether Article 19(9)(c) bars granting an application for registration: some governor has reported a reportable matter to the Commissioner and the issue has not been determined, or a resulting order or notice has not been complied with; the answer is IP23
GIVEN reports IS A LIST OF `Reported matter under Article 19(9)`
        @desc The reports of reportable matters to the Commissioner by governors of the applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` reports MEANS
    any (GIVEN reported YIELD
                reported's `the governor reported the matter to the Commissioner`
            AND (    NOT reported's `the issue has been determined`
                 OR  NOT reported's `any resulting order or notice has been complied with`))
        reports

-- src:502 | (c) must not, in the case of an application for registration, grant that application until the issue has been determined and any resulting order or notice complied with;
@ref Article 19(9)(c) (src:502)
@export Whether the Commissioner must not grant an application for registration until the issue a governor's report raises has been determined and any resulting order or notice complied with
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity
        @desc The entity, with its standing on the register
      `Article 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether Article 19(9)(c) bars granting the application (IP23)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 19`
`Art 19(9)(c) the Commissioner must not grant the application` `the entity` `Article 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` MEANS
    IF       `the entity is an applicant for registration` `the entity`
         AND `Article 19(9)(c) bars granting the application`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         SHANT `grant the application for registration` `the Commissioner`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the Commissioner` BECAUSE "Article 19(9)(c): the application for registration was granted before the issue raised by a governor's report was determined and any resulting order or notice complied with"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:503 | (d) may, in the case of a registered charity, by written notice to the charity, permit, either unconditionally or subject to any condition appearing to the Commissioner to be necessary, the governor to act as a governor until that issue is determined or the notice is withdrawn;
@ref Article 19(9)(d) (src:503)
@export Whether the Commissioner may, by written notice to a registered charity, permit a governor who has reported a reportable matter to act as a governor until the issue is determined or the notice is withdrawn; the conditions are the Commissioner's judgement
GIVEN `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the entity is entered in the general or the restricted section of the register
      reported IS A `Reported matter under Article 19(9)`
        @desc The report of the reportable matter to the Commissioner
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 19`
`Art 19(9)(d) the Commissioner may permit the governor to act until the issue is determined` `the entity is a registered charity` reported MEANS
    IF       `the entity is a registered charity`
         AND reported's `the governor reported the matter to the Commissioner`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MAY   `permit the governor to act as a governor until the issue is determined or the notice is withdrawn` `the Commissioner`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (e): if the issue is not to be determined by the court, then on determining it the Commissioner must do one of two things: (i) in the case of an application, notify the entity that it will be refused unless the governor is
-- removed, or in the case of a registered charity serve a required steps notice requiring the charity to suspend or remove the governor; or (ii) give permission by a notice entered in the register.
-- Whichever is done discharges the duty (they are alternatives), so the duties are composed with ROR; each alternative is an unguarded duty, so that no alternative fulfils the choice by itself.
-- F6.15: for an organized religious charity Article 28(3) makes a required steps notice invalid to the extent that it requires a governor to be suspended or removed.
@ref Article 19(9)(e)(i) (src:505)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 19`
`Art 19(9)(e)(i) the Commissioner must notify the entity that its application will be refused unless the governor is removed` MEANS
    PARTY `the Commissioner`
    MUST  `notify the entity that the application will be refused unless the governor is removed` `the Commissioner`
    HENCE FULFILLED

@ref Article 19(9)(e)(i) (src:505)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 19`
`Art 19(9)(e)(i) the Commissioner must serve a required steps notice requiring the charity to suspend or remove the governor` MEANS
    PARTY `the Commissioner`
    MUST  `serve a required steps notice requiring the charity to suspend or remove the governor` `the Commissioner`
    HENCE FULFILLED

@ref Article 19(9)(e)(ii) (src:506)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 19`
`Art 19(9)(e)(ii) the Commissioner must give permission to act by notice entered in the register` MEANS
    PARTY `the Commissioner`
    MUST  `give permission for the governor to act as a governor by notice entered in the register` `the Commissioner`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- What (e)(i) offers, by kind of entity, on each reading of F6.15.
@ref Article 19(9)(e)(i) (F6.15) (src:505)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      `the entity` IS AN Entity
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 19`
`Art 19(9)(e)(i) the removal alternative of the Commissioner` interp `the entity` `the registered charity` MEANS
    IF   `the entity is an applicant for registration` `the entity`
    THEN `Art 19(9)(e)(i) the Commissioner must notify the entity that its application will be refused unless the governor is removed`
    ELSE CONSIDER interp's `how the duty in Article 19(9)(e)(i) stands against Article 28(3)`
         WHEN `Article 28(3) prevails and no duty to require removal arises for an organized religious charity`
              THEN IF   `the registered charity`'s `is an organized religious charity`
                   THEN `Art 19(9)(e)(ii) the Commissioner must give permission to act by notice entered in the register`
                   ELSE `Art 19(9)(e)(i) the Commissioner must serve a required steps notice requiring the charity to suspend or remove the governor`
         WHEN `the duty stands and the notice is void to the extent that it requires removal`
              THEN `Art 19(9)(e)(i) the Commissioner must serve a required steps notice requiring the charity to suspend or remove the governor`
         WHEN `the two provisions conflict and the Law does not say which prevails`
              THEN IF   `the registered charity`'s `is an organized religious charity`
                   THEN `Art 19(9)(e)(i) the Law does not say whether the Commissioner must serve a notice requiring removal on an organized religious charity`
                   ELSE `Art 19(9)(e)(i) the Commissioner must serve a required steps notice requiring the charity to suspend or remove the governor`

@ref Article 19(9)(e)(i) (src:505) and Article 28(3)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 19`
`Art 19(9)(e)(i) the Law does not say whether the Commissioner must serve a notice requiring removal on an organized religious charity` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 19(9)(e)(i) obliges the Commissioner to serve a required steps notice requiring the charity to suspend or remove the governor, and Article 28(3) makes such a notice invalid for an organized religious charity; the Law does not say which prevails"

-- src:504 | (e) must, if the issue is not to be determined by the court under sub-paragraph (b), on determining the issue –
-- src:505 | (i) notify the entity that the application will be refused unless the governor is removed, or in the case of a registered charity serve a required steps notice requiring the charity to suspend or remove the governor, or
-- src:506 | (ii) by notice in writing, entered in the register, give permission for the governor to act as a governor, either unconditionally or subject to any condition or time limit that appears to the Commissioner to be necessary.
@ref Article 19(9)(e) (src:504-506)
@export Whether and how the Commissioner must, on determining the issue (where the court is not to determine it), either notify the entity that its application will be refused unless the governor is removed, or serve a required steps notice requiring the charity to suspend or remove the governor, or give permission by notice entered in the register; for an organized religious charity the removal alternative depends on the reading of Article 28(3)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
        @desc The readings of the open points of Articles 15 to 20; here F6.15 (the duty in Article 19(9)(e)(i) against Article 28(3))
      `the entity` IS AN Entity
        @desc The entity, with its standing on the register
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity`
        @desc What the register holds about the entity, including whether it is an organized religious charity (IP20)
      reported IS A `Reported matter under Article 19(9)`
        @desc The report of the reportable matter to the Commissioner
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 19`
`Art 19(9)(e) the Commissioner must remove or permit on determining the issue` interp `the entity` `the registered charity` reported MEANS
    IF       reported's `the governor reported the matter to the Commissioner`
         AND NOT reported's `the Commissioner has applied to the court to determine the issue`
    THEN     `Art 19(9)(e)(i) the removal alternative of the Commissioner` interp `the entity` `the registered charity`
         ROR `Art 19(9)(e)(ii) the Commissioner must give permission to act by notice entered in the register`
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§§ `Article 19(10), (11) and (12) -- acting as a governor after reporting; the offence`

-- A permission to act as a governor: who gave it, when, and the days that end it. The days are the last days named in the permission's own terms (the notice's withdrawal, the determination of the issue
-- for a permission under (9)(d), and a time limit); whether the last day named is inside the permission is F6.22.
DECLARE `Source of a permission to act as a governor` IS ONE OF
    `the Commissioner by written notice to the charity under Article 19(9)(d)`
    `the Commissioner by notice entered in the register under Article 19(9)(e)(ii)`
    `the court by an order under Article 20`

DECLARE `Permission to act as a governor` HAS
    source IS A `Source of a permission to act as a governor`
        @desc Who gave the permission, and under which provision
    `given on` IS A DATE
        @desc The day the permission was given
    `withdrawn on` IS A MAYBE DATE
        @desc The day the notice was withdrawn; NOTHING if it has not been
    `the issue is determined on` IS A MAYBE DATE
        @desc For a permission under Article 19(9)(d): the day the issue is determined; NOTHING while it is not
    `time limit ends on` IS A MAYBE DATE
        @desc The last day named in a time limit on the permission; NOTHING if it has none

@ref Article 19(9)(d), (e)(ii) (F6.22) (src:503) (src:506)
GIVEN reading IS A `Reading of the last day of a permission to act as a governor`
      day IS A DATE
      end IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the permission has not ended by the optional day` reading day end MEANS
    CONSIDER end
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST last THEN `the day is within a period whose last day is named` reading day last

@ref Article 19(10)(a) (F6.22) (src:508)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      permission IS A `Permission to act as a governor`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the permission to act as a governor is in force on the day` interp permission day MEANS
        permission's `given on` AT MOST day
    AND `the permission has not ended by the optional day` (interp's `whether the last day named in a time limit is inside the permission`) day (permission's `withdrawn on`)
    AND `the permission has not ended by the optional day` (interp's `whether the last day named in a time limit is inside the permission`) day (permission's `the issue is determined on`)
    AND `the permission has not ended by the optional day` (interp's `whether the last day named in a time limit is inside the permission`) day (permission's `time limit ends on`)

-- F6.10: when the ban starts. "At any time after reporting a reportable matter": the paragraph does not say to whom the report must be made. The reading taken is the report to the Commissioner;
-- the others are the report to the entity or charity, and both reports. A day-granular model cannot place an act before or after a report made the same day, so the day of the report is inside the ban on every reading.
@ref Article 19(10) (F6.10) (src:507)
GIVEN position IS A `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`F6.10 reading A: the ban starts on the report to the Commissioner` position MEANS
    position's `reported to the Commissioner on`

@ref Article 19(10) (F6.10) (src:507)
GIVEN position IS A `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`F6.10 reading B: the ban starts on the report to the entity or charity` position MEANS
    position's `reported to the entity or charity on`

@ref Article 19(10) (F6.10) (src:507)
GIVEN position IS A `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`F6.10 reading C: the ban starts when both reports have been made` position MEANS
    CONSIDER position's `reported to the entity or charity on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST first THEN
        CONSIDER position's `reported to the Commissioner on`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST second THEN JUST (`the later of` first second)

@ref Article 19(10) (F6.10) (src:507)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      position IS A `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day on which the ban of Article 19(10) starts` interp position MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `when the ban of Article 19(10) starts`
    WHEN `the ban starts on the report to the Commissioner`
        THEN `F6.10 reading A: the ban starts on the report to the Commissioner` position
    WHEN `the ban starts on the report to the entity or charity`
        THEN `F6.10 reading B: the ban starts on the report to the entity or charity` position
    WHEN `the ban starts when both reports have been made`
        THEN `F6.10 reading C: the ban starts when both reports have been made` position

@ref Article 19(10) (F6.10) (src:507)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      position IS A `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the ban of Article 19(10) applies on the day` interp position day MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day on which the ban of Article 19(10) starts` interp position
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST start THEN start AT MOST day

-- The ban is lifted, for an act, when the governor is permitted and does the act in accordance with any condition on the permission (limbs (a) AND (b)).
-- src:508 | (a) is permitted to do so by the Commissioner under paragraph (9)(d) or (e)(ii), or by the court under Article 20; and
-- src:509 | (b) does so in either case in accordance with any condition on that permission.
@ref Article 19(10)(a) and (b) (src:508-509)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      permissions IS A LIST OF `Permission to act as a governor`
      day IS A DATE
      `the act is done in accordance with any condition on the permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 19(10) the governor is permitted to act on the day and acts in accordance with any condition` interp permissions day `the act is done in accordance with any condition on the permission` MEANS
        "(a) is permitted to do so by the Commissioner under paragraph (9)(d) or (e)(ii), or by the court under Article 20; and"
    ... any (GIVEN permission YIELD `the permission to act as a governor is in force on the day` interp permission day) permissions
    AND "(b) does so in either case in accordance with any condition on that permission."
    ... `the act is done in accordance with any condition on the permission`

-- Whether the person, acting as a governor on the day, contravenes paragraph (10): the ban applies and the exception does not.
-- src:507 | (10) A person must not act as a governor of a registered charity at any time after reporting a reportable matter, unless the governor –
-- src:508 | (a) is permitted to do so by the Commissioner under paragraph (9)(d) or (e)(ii), or by the court under Article 20; and
-- src:509 | (b) does so in either case in accordance with any condition on that permission.
@ref Article 19(10) (src:507-509)
@export Whether a person who acts as a governor of a registered charity on a given day contravenes Article 19(10): the person has reported a reportable matter (on the reading of when the ban starts) and is not permitted, or does not act in accordance with the condition on the permission
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
        @desc The readings of the open points of Articles 15 to 20; here F6.10 (when the ban starts) and F6.22 (the last day of a permission)
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the entity is entered in the general or the restricted section of the register
      position IS A `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)`
        @desc What the person has reported, and when
      permissions IS A LIST OF `Permission to act as a governor`
        @desc The permissions the person has been given, with the days that end them
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
        @desc The day on which the person acts as a governor
      `the act is done in accordance with any condition on the permission` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the person acts in accordance with any condition on the permission; TRUE if there is none
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` interp `the entity is a registered charity` position permissions `the day in question` `the act is done in accordance with any condition on the permission` MEANS
        `the entity is a registered charity`
    AND `the ban of Article 19(10) applies on the day` interp position `the day in question`
    AND NOT `Art 19(10) the governor is permitted to act on the day and acts in accordance with any condition` interp permissions `the day in question` `the act is done in accordance with any condition on the permission`

-- src:507 | (10) A person must not act as a governor of a registered charity at any time after reporting a reportable matter, unless the governor –
@ref Article 19(10) (src:507)
@export Whether and how a person must not act as a governor of a registered charity at any time after reporting a reportable matter, unless permitted and acting within any condition on the permission; the breach is an offence under Article 19(11) if committed without reasonable excuse
GIVEN `the person contravenes paragraph (10)` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the person, on the day in question, is within the ban of Article 19(10) and not within its exception (the function Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10) answers this)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 19`
`Art 19(10) the person must not act as a governor after reporting` `the person contravenes paragraph (10)` MEANS
    IF   `the person contravenes paragraph (10)`
    THEN PARTY `any person`
         SHANT `act as a governor of a registered charity` `any person`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `any person` BECAUSE "Article 19(10): acted as a governor of a registered charity after reporting a reportable matter, without a permission or outside its condition; an offence under Article 19(11) if without reasonable excuse"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- The prohibition, standing: the ban applies to a person who has reported, and an act as a governor is the failure. This form has no facts to consult and is the one a trace exercises.
@ref Article 19(10) (src:507)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 19`
`Art 19(10) the standing ban on acting as a governor after reporting` MEANS
    PARTY `any person`
    SHANT `act as a governor of a registered charity` `any person`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `any person` BECAUSE "Article 19(10): acted as a governor of a registered charity after reporting a reportable matter, without a permission or outside its condition"

-- The offence: contravening paragraph (10) without reasonable excuse. "Reasonable excuse" is the court's judgement and is an input.
-- src:510 | (11) A person who without reasonable excuse contravenes paragraph (10) commits an offence and is liable to imprisonment for one year and to a fine.
@ref Article 19(11) (src:510)
@export Whether a person commits the offence of Article 19(11): contravenes paragraph (10) without reasonable excuse
GIVEN `the person contravenes paragraph (10)` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the person contravenes Article 19(10)
      `the person has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the person has a reasonable excuse for the contravention
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 19(11) the person commits an offence` `the person contravenes paragraph (10)` `the person has a reasonable excuse` MEANS
        `the person contravenes paragraph (10)`
    AND NOT `the person has a reasonable excuse`

-- The penalty is a ceiling, as data: imprisonment for one year (12 months on the reading taken of the unit, F6.16) and a fine for which the Law states no maximum (so none is invented).
-- src:510 | (11) A person who without reasonable excuse contravenes paragraph (10) commits an offence and is liable to imprisonment for one year and to a fine.
@ref Article 19(11) (src:510)
@export The penalty Article 19(11) provides for the offence: imprisonment for a term of up to 12 months and a fine for which the Law states no maximum; the answer is IP30 for this offence
GIVETH A `Penalty provided`
`Art 19(11) the penalty for contravening Article 19(10)` MEANS
    `Penalty provided` WITH
        `imprisonment up to, in months` IS JUST 12
        fine IS `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`

-- F6.16: "one year". On the reading taken the term is 12 calendar months from its start; on the other it is 365 days.
@ref Article 19(11) (F6.16) (src:510)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      start IS A DATE
      days IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 19(11) a term of days from the start is within the maximum of one year` interp start days MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `how a term of imprisonment of one year or two years is measured`
    WHEN `calendar months` THEN (start PLUS days) AT MOST `add months` start 12
    WHEN `days` THEN days AT MOST 365

-- src:511 | (12) Paragraphs (10) and (11) are not to be construed as requiring an act to be treated as void or invalid merely by virtue of the act constituting a contravention of paragraph (10).
@ref Article 19(12) (src:511)
@export Whether paragraphs (10) and (11) make an act void or invalid merely because it contravened paragraph (10) (they do not)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 19(12) paragraphs (10) and (11) make an act void or invalid merely because it contravened paragraph (10)` MEANS
    FALSE

§§§ `Article 19(13) -- the Commissioner may apply to the court on suspecting a breach of paragraph (2)`

-- src:512 | (13) If at any time the Commissioner suspects that a governor of a registered charity may have breached paragraph (2), the Commissioner may, without prejudice to any other of his or her powers, apply to the court to determine whether the governor is a fit and proper person to be a governor.
@ref Article 19(13) (src:512)
@export Whether the Commissioner may apply to the court to determine whether a governor of a registered charity is a fit and proper person, on suspecting that the governor may have breached Article 19(2)
GIVEN `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the entity is entered in the general or the restricted section of the register
      `the Commissioner suspects that the governor may have breached paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the Commissioner suspects, at that time, that the governor may have breached Article 19(2)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 19`
`Art 19(13) the Commissioner may apply to the court` `the entity is a registered charity` `the Commissioner suspects that the governor may have breached paragraph (2)` MEANS
    IF       `the entity is a registered charity`
         AND `the Commissioner suspects that the governor may have breached paragraph (2)`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MAY   `apply to the court to determine whether the governor is a fit and proper person` `the Commissioner`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED
